---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base title="Alpha Testing Agreement & Terms of Service | Bigby.cloud" description="Bigby.cloud's Alpha Testing Agreement & Terms of Service.">
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="py-5">
      <div class="container" style="max-width: 720px;">

        <h1>Alpha Testing Agreement & Terms of Service</h1>

        <p>This agreement is between <strong>Bigby.cloud Ltd</strong> ("we", "us") and you ("you").</p>

        <h2>1. What this is</h2>
        <p>You are testing an <strong>early alpha version</strong> of our cloud storage and office suite. It is unfinished, potentially buggy, and may change or break at any time. This is not a finished product.</p>

        <h2>2. What we promise (and do not promise)</h2>
        <p>We provide the service <strong>"as is" and "as available"</strong> with no warranty of any kind. We do not guarantee:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>uptime or availability,</li>
            <li>that your data will not be lost or corrupted,</li>
            <li>that the service is secure or free from vulnerabilities,</li>
            <li>that it will work for your specific needs.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To the fullest extent permitted by UK law, we exclude all implied warranties, including merchantability and fitness for purpose.</p>

        <h2>3. What you agree to</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>You will use the service only for testing and evaluation.</li>
            <li>You will provide feedback to us about the service when requested within 30 days.</li>
            <li>You will not use it for critical business operations or as your sole copy of important data.</li>
            <li>You will not upload anything illegal, harmful, or that infringes anyone else's rights.</li>
            <li>You confirm that you have the legal right to upload anything you store, including any personal data about your clients or contacts.</li>
            <li>You will keep your account credentials secure and not share them.</li>
            <li>You will not reverse-engineer, scrape, or attempt to break the service.</li>
            <li>You agree that details of this alpha test, including screenshots, feature descriptions, and performance observations, are <strong>confidential</strong> and you will not share them publicly or with third parties without our written permission.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Your content and intellectual property</h2>
        <p>You own the files and data you upload. We do not claim ownership of your content. You grant us a licence to store, host, and process your content solely to run the service for you.</p>
        <p>You grant us a perpetual, royalty-free licence to use any feedback, bug reports, or suggestions you provide to improve our products.</p>
        <p>We own all intellectual property in the service itself, including code, design, and branding.</p>

        <h2>5. Liability</h2>
        <p>Because this is an alpha test, our liability is strictly limited.</p>
        <p>Our total liability to you for any claim arising out of this agreement shall not exceed the total amount you paid us in the <strong>12 months before the claim</strong>, or <strong>£1</strong> if you have not paid anything.</p>
        <p>We are not liable for, unless caused by our wilful misconduct:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>loss of profits, revenue, or business,</li>
            <li>loss of data,</li>
            <li>indirect or consequential loss,</li>
            <li>any loss caused by your failure to keep backups.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Nothing in this agreement limits our liability for fraud, death, or personal injury caused by our negligence.</p>

        <h2>6. Termination</h2>
        <p>Either of us can terminate this agreement at any time, for any reason, with immediate effect by notifying the other. We may also suspend your access immediately if you misuse the service or breach this agreement.</p>
        <p>When the agreement ends, we will delete or return your data in line with our Privacy Notice.</p>

        <h2>7. Data protection</h2>
        <p>The way we handle personal data is set out in our Privacy Policy. If you upload personal data about your own clients or contacts, we act as a <strong>processor</strong> for that data and our <strong>Data Processing Agreement</strong> applies.</p>

        <h2>8. General</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>This agreement is governed by the laws of <strong>England and Wales</strong>.</li>
            <li>If any part of this agreement is unenforceable, the rest remains in force.</li>
            <li>This is the entire agreement between us about the alpha test.</li>
        </ul>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
